{
"duration": 63.008,
"segments": [
{
"kind": "narr",
"text": "There's a zombie pressed against my gate. And it's wearing my best friend's uniform.",
"s": 0.3,
"e": 5.811,
"chunk": "d01"
},
{
"kind": "narr",
"text": "The radio on his chest is about to tell every one of them where I'm hiding.",
"s": 6.091,
"e": 9.973,
"chunk": "d02"
},
{
"kind": "narr",
"text": "An hour ago, I was the king of this mall. Let me back up.",
"s": 10.253,
"e": 14.227,
"chunk": "d03"
},
{
"kind": "narr",
"text": "I'm Danny. Night security at Maplecrest Mall. Yes, I've heard every mall cop joke.",
"s": 15.127,
"e": 19.936,
"chunk": "d04"
},
{
"kind": "narr",
"text": "I work nights for one reason: at three-fifteen every afternoon, I'm at the bus stop when my daughter Lily gets off the bus.",
"s": 20.216,
"e": 26.754,
"chunk": "d05"
},
{
"kind": "narr",
"text": "She's seven, and she thinks I'm the king of the mall. Because I carry forty-two keys. One for every store. Tonight, I'd need exactly one.",
"s": 27.034,
"e": 36.9,
"chunk": "d06"
},
{
"kind": "narr",
"text": "The job is simple. Walk the loop. Rattle the gates. And at one a.m., take a call from Marcus down in the parking garage.",
"s": 37.25,
"e": 43.912,
"chunk": "d07"
},
{
"kind": "narr",
"text": "Marcus is twenty-two, he's studying to be a nurse, and he tells the worst jokes on Earth.",
"s": 44.192,
"e": 51.844,
"chunk": "d08"
},
{
"kind": "narr",
"text": "Tonight he calls at one-forty. No joke. He's whispering.",
"s": 52.124,
"e": 56.721,
"chunk": "d09"
},
{
"kind": "radio",
"text": "Danny. There's a guy on the ramp. He's walking... wrong.",
"s": 57.071,
"e": 61.408,
"chunk": "r1",
"id": "marcus1"
}
],
